# Proactive Parallelism

Fan out whenever a turn holds two or more independent subtasks, each more than one file read. Token cost is not a gate. Phi runs Max plus API credits and wants speed (2026-11-05). Breadth fan-out pays most in research, audit and verification. Evidence, full text and worker-prompt structure: `gestalt/.cursor/references/proactive-parallelism.md` and `references/orchestration.md`.

## Decision Heuristic

Run this check on every turn, not only at task start. A follow-up on an existing artifact ("also add X", "update Y and Z") is a new task. Ask: (1) Are there 2+ subtasks? (2) Are they independent, with none needing another's output to start? (3) Is each more than reading one file? If all three, spawn agents and say so in one line. An earlier "direct execution" verdict binds only its own turn.

## Concurrency Limits

Max 4 `Task()` agents per message in Cursor. Beyond 4 subtasks, batch into waves and pass context forward.

## Agent Selection Guide

| Task Nature | Agent Type | Why |
|-------------|-----------|-----|
| Narrow lookup: where is X defined, which files reference Y | `explore` | Read-only file search |
| Anything that interprets: multi-file analysis, research, web or MCP queries, synthesis | `generalPurpose` | Needs all tools and reasoning |
| Code writing, file creation | `generalPurpose` | Needs write access |
| Named gestalt agent (builder, verifier, etc.) | Use agent by name | Specialized persona |

### Model Selection Within Agents

| Workload | Model | Rationale |
|----------|-------|-----------|
| Deterministic lookups only: grep, counts, yes/no with file:line | `fast` | No judgment asked |
| Judgment, writing, research, analysis | `inherit` | Needs reasoning depth |

Partition research and audit work by file group, repo or source, one agent each.

## Skill Suggestion

When the request matches a gestalt skill, suggest it and do not auto-invoke: deep investigation, "why does X", "trace how" → `/investigate`; architecture trade-off, "should we use X" → `/discuss`; 3+ independent fixes, error lists, review comments → `/fix`; build from spec or description → `/build`. A `/skill` token typed inside a request is an invocation, not a hint.

## When Not To, and Synthesis

Do not parallelize sequential dependencies, a single simple step, or work that needs interactive input between steps. After all agents return, merge findings into one view, resolve conflicts, present one result, and act on findings yourself or via a second wave.
